# Wave W17-AB (Route 225): zone pine — a tough SPARSE-crowned pine in dusty grey-greens, its tiers narrow and its highlight dust-pale, on scorch turf (ground baked in): a tree that trains like everything else on this road — lean, hard, and still unmistakably a tree, its canopy fat enough to read at a glance and its tiers open to the heat. Route 225’s own tree — split from Route 224’s head pine by crown entire (sparse dust-green vs full coast green) and from Route 227’s ash-dusted pine ahead of the program by cover: this crown is dusty from the ground up, that one is dusted from the sky down.
